## Auth flow

- App starts unauthenticated (`activeAccount = null`) → `SignInScreen` shown
- Clicking an account row calls `signIn(id)` → calendar renders immediately
- Avatar in `TopBar` shows current account initials + color; clicking opens `ProfileMenu`
- "Sign out" in `ProfileMenu` calls `signOut()` → back to `SignInScreen`
- "Switch account" in `ProfileMenu` calls `switchAccount(id)` → same calendar, new identity
- Session is in-memory only — page refresh resets to unauthenticated

## AuthGate pattern

`client/App.tsx` renders an `AuthGate` component inside `BrowserRouter`:


function AuthGate() {
  const { activeAccount } = useAuth();
  return activeAccount ? <Index /> : <SignInScreen />;
}
```

`AuthProvider` wraps the entire app (outside `BrowserRouter`).

## TopBar avatar

`TopBar` reads `useAuth().activeAccount` to display dynamic initials and color.
`profileMenuOpen` state controls whether `ProfileMenu` is shown.
The avatar div has `role="button"`, `aria-label="Account"`, `tabIndex={0}`, keyboard support.
When `profileMenuOpen` is true, a 2px primary outline ring is applied to the avatar.
